EXT. SALT FLATS, ABANDONED SURVEY CAMP - DAWN

White to every horizon. A crooked tent. A dead mule on its side. Heat already shimmers.

TOBIAS GRAYSON, forties, leathered, sits against the tent pole, a bullet in his gut, his hat over his eyes. LENORE BASQUIAT, thirty, in a duster, kneels with a canteen. Two outlaws, the SLATER BROTHERS, JUDE and ABEL, stand over them, rifles lowered.

JUDE
He's done.

LENORE
He's breathing.

ABEL
Not for long.

TOBIAS
(thin)
Leave her out of it.

JUDE
She dug your claim.

LENORE
It was never his claim.

ABEL
Then whose?

LENORE
Mine.

Silence. Jude lifts his rifle again, slowly. Abel holds out a hand.

ABEL (CONT'D)
Let her talk.

TOBIAS
Lenore. Don't.

LENORE
It's under the mule.

The brothers look at the dead animal. Tobias's hand slips from his gut. The canteen falls and the water drains into the salt.
